    "policy_implications": {
      "pension": "Only 3.8% of Tanzanian adults have pension coverage. 32,833,700 people — including virtually the entire Legacy Stage — have no formal retirement income and no existing TRA relationship through pension systems. Legacy Stage interventions cannot rely on pension records as a touchpoint and must build the relationship from scratch.",
      "insurance": "Only 9.6% of Tanzanian adults have insurance. The Asset Stage population has no formal financial protection and no existing formal relationship that TRA can use as an entry point. Asset Stage interventions must lead with value — offering something before asking for compliance — because there is no existing trust relationship to draw on."
